Subject: Derived CPMS I03 Semantic Residual and Conformance Source

Description: Manager-derived technical source following proven CPMS-I02 canonical documents. It preserves the residual-registry, byte-ingress, independent-validation, and schema-serde conformance question before SJS refinement and grants no implementation authority by itself.

@ [source_uuid] e5b27343-d795-445e-9992-84c2347ae5d4
@ [source_kind] manager_derived_technical_question
@ [baseline_commit] 96113bf024b0dd9d50464cbdfb91db1a80aede59

& [KnownInput] is the completed CPMS-I02 result
  + five self-contained direction-qualified Draft 2020-12 documents and one deterministic bundle are checked in with exact bytes digests local closures resource accounts and checkpoint-A lineage
  + documents describe actual strict serde transport forms but do not yet independently test validation agreement over supplied instances
  + existing root and definition metadata names six recursive-machine-schema residual ids but does not define a complete executable residual catalogue
  + JSON Schema syntax serde structural decoding Cantor semantic validation and authority admission are constitutionally distinct gates

& [IngressQuestion] is how to preserve facts that serde_json Value would erase
  + accept bounded supplied UTF-8 JSON bytes rather than assuming a pre-parsed Value is faithful evidence
  + reject malformed JSON invalid UTF-8 trailing data and duplicate object keys at every nesting depth before instance validation
  + produce one immutable parsed value only after the complete byte input passes
  + record byte length structural depth aggregate object members array items scalar count and duplicate-key disposition under finite limits
  + never resolve a schema reference through HTTP filesystem environment provider or caller-supplied retriever

& [ValidatorQuestion] is how to add an independent syntax judge safely
  + pin one Draft 2020-12 engine under an exact dependency and lock review
  + compile only the checked-in canonical documents after their expected path length digest id dialect and local-reference closure are reverified
  + disable default HTTP and file retrieval features and reject every nonlocal reference before validator construction
  + meta-schema validity validator construction and instance validation are separate dispositions
  + normalize engine diagnostics into bounded deterministic Cantor records without claiming engine message bytes as a stable public protocol

& [ResidualQuestion] is how to name everything syntax cannot prove
  + each residual requires a stable id intended subject condition classification enforcement stage exact enforcing function or explicit unimplemented marker severity proof references and covered schema roots
  + distinguish structural serde-only behavior cross-field value rules digest correspondence referential integrity causal replay resource enforcement authority admission and declared non-capability
  + every residual id referenced by a schema document must resolve exactly once in the registry
  + registry completeness means every known non-syntactic acceptance condition on the five public roots is represented at the selected release baseline; it does not claim discovery of all possible future invariants
  + schema acceptance cannot discharge a residual and an unimplemented residual cannot be represented as passed

& [ConformanceQuestion] is two independent readers over one faithful input
  + each immutable case binds a case id root kind direction supplied bytes expected byte-parser schema serde and optional semantic dispositions plus rationale and residual references
  + schema validation consumes the duplicate-preserving parser result only after byte ingress succeeds
  + serde decoding independently consumes the original exact bytes into the actual root type
  + agreement is required only for a syntax rule explicitly claimed common to schema and serde
  + positive minimum maximum missing null unknown duplicate wrong-type wrong-tag wrong-enum excessive-cardinality and recursive-depth cases are required where the root can express them
  + disagreements are typed release-blocking findings with both observations preserved
  + semantic execution occurs only for complete safe fixtures and remains distinct from syntax agreement

& [CorpusQuestion] is how to make proof finite representative and reproducible
  + cases are checked-in declarative fixtures or pure in-memory constructions with fixed ids exact root assignment and deterministic lexical order
  + every schema keyword and serde attribute behavior claimed by I02 receives at least one positive and one negative witness when a negative is constructible
  + boundary families use below at and above values without attempting exhaustive proof over infinite inputs
  + corpus cases and bytes remain under the previously formed limits of 4096 cases and 67108864 aggregate bytes
  + coverage accounts identify root kind rule class schema path residual ids and observed outcomes without converting test coverage into production qualification

& [DependencyQuestion] is separately signable
  + jsonschema 0.49.2 is a candidate because it supports Draft 2020-12 and meta-schema validation under Rust 1.85 or later
  + its default feature set enables HTTP and file resolution and therefore cannot be admitted unchanged
  + exact no-default-feature resolution offline cache status transitive dependency change audit and Application Control execution remain activation prerequisites
  + a local duplicate-rejecting serde visitor is preferable to a second general parser if it can prove recursive duplicate refusal and exact Value equivalence without hidden normalization

& [FaultQuestion] is fail closed and inspectable
  + no parsed value validator residual registry corpus report or semantic disposition is released partially after any failed prerequisite
  + syntax invalid semantic invalid authority refused unimplemented exhausted internal fault and conformance disagreement remain different classes
  + engine panic nondeterministic diagnostic dependence unresolved reference stale schema stale residual or exceeded resource stops the slice

& [SliceQuestion] is separately governed
  + form exact ingress validator residual corpus comparison resource fault and proof contracts for CPMS-I03
  - never: implement during formation, contact network or filesystem at runtime, accept external schema retrieval, classify changed schemas for compatibility, define provider tools, call a model, persist runtime state, perform semantic effect, claim production, or implement hardware
